  "name": "Kept at Golden Hour",
  "premise": "A sealed glass garden where the sun has been stopped just above the horizon so that nothing inside will ever have to end. Whoever put the glass over it did it out of tenderness. The plants have grown toward that one light for so long they have forgotten there are others; the dreamer is the first thing in here that still remembers dusk. Every space asks the same thing: is keeping a kindness, and what does it cost the kept.",
