   "summary": "The peach hall has dissolved into sand: you are a small thing inside a vast terrarium on a windowsill, with the sun stopped a finger above the horizon and five tall heliotropes straining toward it. Stand still near a flower and it slowly forgets the sun and turns to watch you instead; when all five have turned away, nothing is holding the sun up and it finally sets. In the dark, cold leaks in through a glowing crack in the glass on the far side; walking into it is the way onward.",
